$DIR/main.p:8:7: the operand of or is not a single call
    An or clause tests the error that a call returns, so or must come right
    after a call: a function, method or function value with its arguments. Here
    something else is in front of or: an operator, parentheses, a selector, or a
    list of values. Such an operand could hide which call's error the clause
    tests.
    Make the call alone the operand of or, and use its values in a statement
    after it:
        n := strconv.Atoi(s) or return
        total := n + 1
    (see "Or clauses" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.27)
    (run "pluto explain E1013" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:9:7: the operand of or is a call in parentheses; write the call without them
    (explained above; run "pluto explain E1013" for more)

$DIR/main.p:10:7: the operand of or is not a call; or must directly follow the call whose error it tests
    (explained above; run "pluto explain E1013" for more)

$DIR/main.p:12:2: or must be on the line where its call ends: a newline after the call ends the statement
    The parser could not read this part of the file as Plutonium. The message
    says what it expected and what it found instead. The mistake is often just
    before the position shown, such as a missing bracket or operator on the line
    before.
    (see "Grammar" in the Plutonium spec, section E)
    (run "pluto explain E1000" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:13:14: expected end of statement, found or: an or clause follows only a call that stands alone or is on the right of = or :=
    The parser expected one thing here and found another. The mistake is often
    just before the position shown: a missing comma, bracket or operator, or a
    keyword used as a name.
    (see "Grammar" in the Plutonium spec, section E)
    (run "pluto explain E1001" for a longer explanation)
